# tiny_cave.dat benchmark script — SQ-1428.
#
# One command per line; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are skipped
# by `cargo run -p lanthorn-scott --example bench` and must be stripped before
# the same script is fed to ScottFree (see README.md for the exact command).
#
# Ten commands that leave the game exactly where they found it. The map is
# three rooms in a line — clearing (1) down to cave (2) down to grotto (3) —
# so down/down/up/up is a closed circuit, and the remaining commands exercise
# the verb/noun matcher, the occurrence pass and the action table without
# changing anything that persists: `get lamp` answers "You already have that."
# from lap two, `rub lamp` re-reveals an idol that is already revealed, and
# `push button` / `pull lever` / `score` / `count` only print.
#
# `drop idol` is deliberately absent: dropping the idol in the clearing is how
# tiny_cave is WON, and a benchmark that wins on lap one measures a quit loop
# from then on. `script_never_ends_the_game` in `crates/scott/examples/bench.rs`
# asserts ten laps' worth of turns are all played, which is what holds that.
get lamp
go down
go down
rub lamp
push button
pull lever
go up
go up
score
count
